 "description": "Proctor2016 - Circadian rhythm of PTH and the dynamics of signaling molecules on bone remodeling\nBioModels BIOMD0000000612 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000612_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 100000 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000612_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: still changing at cap), sampling 100.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): MISMATCH_PARTIAL, max |difference| = 1.00e+00 of species peak (worst: X)\nIndependent check of this deck (SciPy integration with Kintecus semantics) against the SBML: max |difference| = 1.00e+00 of species peak.\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [blocker] event 'AddLOAD1' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [blocker] event 'AddLOAD2' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [blocker] event 'AddPTH1' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [blocker] event 'AddPTH2' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [info] Ocy_I_bound_by_PTH: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Inactivation_of_Wnt_by_Sost: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] MSC_differentiation_to_Ob_pro: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] Osteoblast_progenitor_differentiation_by_Tgfb: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Ob_p_binding_by_PTH: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Ob_maturation_to_Ocy_by_Tgfb: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Ob_m_bound_by_PTH: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Ob_m_apoptosis: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Ob_m_PTH_apoptosis: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] HSC_differentiation_to_Ocl_p: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] MCSF_secretion_by_MSC: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] RANKL_secretion_by_MSCs: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] CREB_activation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\nRenamed species (Kintecus name = SBML id): Source1 = Source; Sink1 = Sink",
